intent: >
  Promote City from optional to required on the homepage contact form so
  Steve can qualify leads against his focus areas (Tustin, Orange, Villa
  Park) without chasing form submissions that lack location context.

slice: "?/?"
kind: feature
behavior_change: additive

reversibility: trivial

scope:
  declared:
    - src/index.njk
  actual:
    - src/index.njk
  drift: []

proof:
  tests_run: "Manual: dev server + Chrome. Verified single city field (no duplicate), required attribute present, label shows 'City *', city sits outside the optional <details> block, ZIP also moved up but stays optional, all other field requirements unchanged."
  result: green
  failing: 0

tests:
  needed: "no"
  rationale: >
    Single attribute change plus moving two fields out of a collapsed
    block. Verified by DOM inspection.

assumptions:
  - "Steve's focus-area qualification benefits more from required-city than the abandonment cost hurts. Locked decision from him; if conversion drops in the next 30 days, the assumption may need revisiting."
  - "City + ZIP visually paired in a 2-col grid matches the original (pre-trim) form layout. Familiar pattern for the visitor."
  - "ZIP staying optional is fine. Steve mentioned city; ZIP was not in scope. If Steve later wants ZIP required too, single attribute flip."

specifications:
  - "Required visible fields on the homepage form: name, city, message, and at least one of phone/email."
  - "ZIP, address, service type, and referral source stay optional in the 'Add project details' collapse."
  - "City label includes the * convention used by other required fields on the form."
  - "City and ZIP visually paired in a 2-col grid (original form layout)."

deviations_from_plan: >
  No plan file. Ad-hoc one-line directive from Steve via Tommy: 'make
  the city mandatory on the customer form'. Followed exactly.

trade_offs: >
  Original form trim (PR #8) cut required fields from 9 to 2 specifically
  because 87 form_starts -> 14 form_submits = 16% conversion, with most
  abandons attributed to field count. Adding city back to required adds
  one field of friction. Steve's judgment is that losing out-of-area
  leads at form time is cheaper than chasing them after submit. Worth
  watching the conversion rate over the next 30 days.

  Could have parsed city from the message field with a simple regex
  match against Orange County city names, but that's a guess against
  free-text input. Required dropdown or required input is cleaner and
  matches Steve's actual qualification workflow.

  Could have made city required via a Stimulus controller validator (like
  phone-or-email) instead of HTML required. Chose HTML required because
  it's simpler and the browser-native UX for required field validation
  is familiar to older visitors.

interfaces: {}

self_review:
  consistency: >
    City and ZIP pair markup mirrors the (now removed) pair that was
    inside the details block. Same Tailwind class vocabulary, same
    2-col grid. Required attribute follows the same pattern as name
    and message.
  metz: N/A — Nunjucks template.
  body_plan: >
    Form's job is unchanged: collect enough info to qualify and contact a
    lead. The required surface grew by one field. The collapsed-details
    block lost two fields (city and zip moved up), making it shorter,
    which is fine. No new objects, no new collaborators.
  honesty: >
    City required with the * label. No hidden coercion. Visitors see the
    requirement before they hit submit.

confidence: high
reviewer_attention:
  - "src/index.njk:687-696 (the new visible city+zip row) — placement between phone/email and message. Worth a glance to confirm the form flows naturally top to bottom."
